["decision","DOCS-S5",1780753012,"codex-worker",{"topic":"arm validate scope behavior: show all-story vs. scoped-only warnings","choice":"all-story warnings by default (by design)","rationale":"DAG hygiene is a repo-wide invariant, not per-story. Allowing warnings from other stories to be ignored would enable DAG decay — the same way ignoring failing tests is unacceptable. The --scope flag exists for focused review but does not excuse ignoring the full-repo signal. Coordinator friction item 4 (unscoped validate is noisy) is rejected: the noise is the feature. Instead, DOCS-S5-T4 adds an explicit DAG hygiene mandate to all agent skills.","affects":["internal/validate/validate.go"]}]
